TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` hooks with a scope enum, plus class-level lifecycle via `IAsyncInitializer` / `IAsyncDisposable` on fixtures. Here's a sketch for each scope:

## 1. Before every test in a class

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // Runs before each [Test] in this class
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs after each [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void SomeTest() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once before/after all tests in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // Runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // Runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void Test1() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> **Note:** `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods must be **static**.

## 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // Runs once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // Runs once after all tests in this assembly
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it automatically.

## 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

```csharp
public class TestSessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // Runs once at the very start of the test run
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // Runs once at the very end of the test run
    }
}
```

---

## Summary table

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Context parameter |
|-------|-----------|----------------|-------------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance | — (optional `TestContext`) |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **static** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Test session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** | `TestSessionContext` |

All hook enums come from `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` (or qualify as `HookType.Test`, etc.).
